# tea2unit: Tea v2 FUser wrap + tick re-arm + TaskQuit scan under a pty.
#
# Frame trace (each repaint is ONE write; first paint hides the cursor;
# repaints address rows ABSOLUTELY — \e[1;1H + \e[2K + text, no \r\n):
#   resize probe (sync, first)  \e[?25l \e[2Ktick=0\r\n
#   tick 1 (sleep 50 -> FUser)  \e[1;1H\e[2Ktick=1
#   tick 2 (re-armed sleep)     \e[1;1H\e[2Ktick=2
#   tick 3 -> quit              \e[?25h + exit 0   (no repaint: hasQuit scan)
# The tick count is DETERMINISTIC (each Tick re-arms exactly one sleep and the
# app quits on the third), so the needles assert the exact frames — unlike the
# spinner animation this is not an unbounded frame stream.
expect \e[?25l
expect tick=0
expect tick=1
expect tick=2
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
